        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Normalize deep link scheme and host",
        "body": "Closes #2\r\n\r\n## Summary\r\n\r\nFixes case-sensitive deep link dispatch in `AppMain`.\r\n\r\n`application(_:open:)` now lowercases both the URL scheme and host before matching, so links such as `Nameplate://config`, `nameplate://Config` and `Nameplate://Settings` are routed correctly instead of being silently ignored.\r\n\r\nThis keeps AppMain consistent with `ConfigProposal`, which already normalizes scheme and host internally.\r\n\r\n## Verification\r\n\r\n- `swift build`\r\n- `git diff --check`\r\n\r\nManual runtime proof, using a temporary local proof hook that invoked the real `AppDelegate.application(_:open:)` handler with `Nameplate://Settings` and logged the AppMain dispatch path. The proof hook and logging were removed after the run and are not part of this PR.\r\n\r\nObserved output:\r\n\r\n```text\r\nPROOF received rawScheme=Nameplate rawHost=Settings\r\nPROOF normalized scheme=nameplate host=settings\r\nPROOF dispatch=settings\r\n```\r\nThis shows a mixed-case deep link reaches AppMain with raw mixed-case values, is normalized to scheme=nameplate and host=settings, and dispatches to the settings branch.",
